          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em weighted limit
            (also called
            %em indexed limit
            or
            %em mean cotensor product
            in older texts) is naturally understood from the point of view on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            as described at
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable functor
          %p
            Weighted limits make sense and are considered in the general context of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V=
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            for the moment, in order to motivate the concept.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            which indexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrams"} diagrams
            over which we want to consider limits and eventually weighted limits. Notice that for
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F \colon K \to Set
          %p
            a
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is canonically identified simply with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            of
            %a{:href => "cone#ConesOverADiagram"} cones
            with tip the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
            set
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi pt
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pt = \{\bullet\}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi lim
                  %mi F
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi K
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Δ
                  %mi pt
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  lim F \;=\; [K,Set](\Delta pt, F)
                  \\,.
          %p This means, more generally, that for
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F \,\colon\, K \to C
          %p
            a functor with values in an arbitrary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "-wise" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi K
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi F
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C\big(-,F(-)\big)
                  \\,\colon\,
                  K
                  \\overset{F}{\longrightarrow}
                  C
                  \\overset{Y}{\longrightarrow}
                  Set^{C^{op}}
          %p can be expressed by the right hand side of:
          #eq:ConicalLimitInWeightedLimitForm.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi K
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi K
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                  %mi Δ
                  %mi pt
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underset{
                  \\underset{k \in K}{\longleftarrow}
                  }{lim}
                  C\big(-,F(k)\big)
                  \\;=\;
                  [K,Set]\Big(
                  \\Delta pt
                  ,\,
                  C\big(-,F(-)\big)
                  \\Big)
                  \\,.
          %p
            (This is the limit over the diagram
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\big(-,F(-)\big) \,\colon\, K \to Set^{C^{op}}
            which, if
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %a{:href => "representable+functor#ExampleLimits"} this example
            at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable functor
          %p
            The
            %strong idea
            of weighted limits is to:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                allow in the formula
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ConicalLimitInWeightedLimitForm"} (1)
                the particular functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi pt
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta pt
                to be replaced by any other functor
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi K
                        %mo →
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \,\colon\, K \to Set
            %li
              %p
                to generalize everything straightforwardly from the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
                context to arbitrary
                = succeed "-enriched" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            The idea is that the weight
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \colon K \to V
            encodes the way in which one generalizes the concept of a
            %a{:href => "cone#ConesOverADiagram"} cones
            over a diagram
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            (that is, something with just a tip from which morphisms are emanating down to
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limits"} homotopy limits
            discussed below, with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            being
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimpSet"} SimpSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphisms"} 1-morphisms
            are emanating from the tip, but that any triangle formed by these is filled by a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-cell
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-morphism"} 3-cell
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+category"} closed
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "," do
